1
00:00:01,376 --> 00:00:02,419
Mmm.

2
00:00:02,461 --> 00:00:03,712
Hey.
Hi.

3
00:00:03,754 --> 00:00:06,005
You have to got to try
this cheesecake.

4
00:00:06,047 --> 00:00:07,341
Oh, you know

5
00:00:07,382 --> 00:00:09,426
I'm not that much
of a sweet tooth.

6
00:00:09,468 --> 00:00:10,928
( mumbling )

7
00:00:10,970 --> 00:00:12,638
Oh, my God, it's so creamy.

8
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:13,931
Oh, my God

9
00:00:13,973 --> 00:00:16,266
that is the best cheesecake
I've ever had.

10
00:00:16,308 --> 00:00:17,935
Where did you get this?

11
00:00:17,977 --> 00:00:21,062
It was at the front door
when I got home.

12
00:00:21,104 --> 00:00:22,815
Somebody sent it to us.

13
00:00:22,857 --> 00:00:25,818
Chandler, this is not
addressed to you.

14
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:28,445
This is addressed
to Mrs. Braverman downstairs.

15
00:00:28,487 --> 00:00:29,446
( gasps )

16
00:00:29,488 --> 00:00:30,781
Thief.

17
00:00:30,823 --> 00:00:33,367
I... I didn't read the
box before I opened it

18
00:00:33,408 --> 00:00:35,035
and you can't
return a box

19
00:00:35,076 --> 00:00:36,704
after you've
opened the box.

20
00:00:36,745 --> 00:00:37,746
Why not?

21
00:00:37,788 --> 00:00:40,248
Because it's too delicious.

22
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:43,168
Chandler, you stole
this cheesecake.

23
00:00:43,210 --> 00:00:44,378
That is wrong.

24
00:00:44,419 --> 00:00:46,296
No, no, no,
it is going to be okay

25
00:00:46,338 --> 00:00:49,675
because Mrs. Braverman is going
to send away for a free one

26
00:00:49,717 --> 00:00:51,385
and that way we all win.

27
00:00:51,426 --> 00:00:55,347
The only losers are the big
cheesecake conglomerate...

28
00:00:55,389 --> 00:00:59,059
"Mama's Little Bakery."

29
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:00,769
I feel terrible.

30
00:01:00,811 --> 00:01:03,271
I'm a horrible, horrible,
horrible person.

31
00:01:03,313 --> 00:01:06,567
Mmm... I'm sorry, what?

32
00:01:13,073 --> 00:01:18,078
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

33
00:01:18,119 --> 00:01:20,288
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

34
00:01:20,330 --> 00:01:23,291
♪ Your love life's DOA ♪

35
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:27,421
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

36
00:01:27,462 --> 00:01:30,758
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

37
00:01:30,799 --> 00:01:33,052
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

38
00:01:33,092 --> 00:01:36,388
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

39
00:01:36,430 --> 00:01:42,519
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

40
00:01:47,399 --> 00:01:48,984
All right,
I should get going.

41
00:01:49,026 --> 00:01:50,027
Big day at work.

42
00:01:50,069 --> 00:01:52,279
You know I'm in coma?

43
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:54,406
Well, today
they do this test on me

44
00:01:54,448 --> 00:01:56,408
and turns out
I'm not brain-dead.

45
00:01:56,450 --> 00:01:58,493
So...

46
00:01:58,535 --> 00:02:00,245
Ah, ah, ah, Mr. Smarty-Pants

47
00:02:00,287 --> 00:02:02,915
it's just my character
that's not brain-dead.

48
00:02:04,625 --> 00:02:06,167
So, Pheebs,
we still on for tonight?

49
00:02:06,209 --> 00:02:07,544
Absolutely.

50
00:02:07,586 --> 00:02:09,088
All right, I'll
see you at 8:00.
Okay.

51
00:02:09,128 --> 00:02:10,297
Oh, what's at 8:00?

52
00:02:10,338 --> 00:02:11,882
Oh, I have dinner plans
with Joey.

53
00:02:11,924 --> 00:02:13,592
We get together
about once a month

54
00:02:13,634 --> 00:02:15,218
to discuss the rest of you guys.

55
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:17,679
Wow, did not know that.

56
00:02:17,721 --> 00:02:21,516
May I say how lovely
you look today?

57
00:02:21,558 --> 00:02:22,684
Duly noted.

58
00:02:22,726 --> 00:02:25,646
Oh, so for tomorrow

59
00:02:25,687 --> 00:02:26,730
do you want
to rent a car

60
00:02:26,772 --> 00:02:28,273
and drive down
together, or what?

61
00:02:28,315 --> 00:02:29,900
What are you
talking about?

62
00:02:29,942 --> 00:02:32,069
Cousin Frannie's wedding;
it's tomorrow night.

63
00:02:32,111 --> 00:02:35,530
You were invited?

64
00:02:35,572 --> 00:02:38,951
No.

65
00:02:38,993 --> 00:02:40,828
Oh, my God,
I can't believe this.

66
00:02:40,869 --> 00:02:42,287
I knew that
mom and dad were invited

67
00:02:42,329 --> 00:02:43,497
but I thought that was it.

68
00:02:43,538 --> 00:02:45,833
I mean, from the ages
of seven to nine

69
00:02:45,874 --> 00:02:47,835
Frannie and I
were inseparable.

70
00:02:47,876 --> 00:02:49,878
Well, maybe since
the age of nine

71
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:51,964
Frannie's made some new friends.

72
00:02:52,006 --> 00:02:54,215
Well... it's probably
just a mistake.

73
00:02:54,257 --> 00:02:56,051
Let me call
Aunt Cheryl, okay?

74
00:02:56,093 --> 00:02:57,427
Maybe you are invited

75
00:02:57,469 --> 00:03:00,179
and the invitation just
got lost in the mail.

76
00:03:00,221 --> 00:03:02,349
Yeah... you call her
and tell her that

77
00:03:02,390 --> 00:03:03,851
you know,
when we were kids

78
00:03:03,892 --> 00:03:05,184
her precious little Frannie

79
00:03:05,226 --> 00:03:07,186
tried to undress me
several times, okay?

80
00:03:07,228 --> 00:03:08,689
And if I
hadn't have stopped her

81
00:03:08,730 --> 00:03:10,691
there probably wouldn't
even be a wedding to go to.

82
00:03:10,732 --> 00:03:13,944
She tried to
undress me, too.

83
00:03:13,986 --> 00:03:17,196
I used to undress
my cousin Glenn.

84
00:03:17,238 --> 00:03:18,782
( chuckles )

85
00:03:23,829 --> 00:03:26,498
Joseph Francis Tribbiani

86
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:28,458
are you home yet?

87
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:30,711
Um, I think
he's still out.
What's wrong?

88
00:03:30,752 --> 00:03:32,504
Well, I'll tell you,
Rachel Karen Green.

89
00:03:32,546 --> 00:03:33,881
I had plans

90
00:03:33,922 --> 00:03:34,882
with Joey tonight

91
00:03:34,923 --> 00:03:36,424
and he left me this note.

92
00:03:36,466 --> 00:03:38,760
"Pheebs, can't make it.

93
00:03:38,802 --> 00:03:41,847
"Got a date.
Talk to you later.

94
00:03:41,889 --> 00:03:42,973
Big Daddy."

95
00:03:43,015 --> 00:03:44,432
Big Daddy?

96
00:03:44,474 --> 00:03:46,143
Oh, that's a nickname
we were trying out.

97
00:03:46,185 --> 00:03:49,228
Hey, you know what nickname
never caught on?

98
00:03:49,270 --> 00:03:50,605
"The Ross-a-tron."

99
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:54,109
Hey.

100
00:03:54,151 --> 00:03:55,569
Oh, here's Joseph Francis.

101
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:57,071
Hey, way... oh...

102
00:03:57,112 --> 00:03:59,907
What are you middle
naming me for?

103
00:03:59,948 --> 00:04:01,491
I left you a note.

104
00:04:01,533 --> 00:04:04,078
So, what? That doesn't give you
the right to ditch me.

105
00:04:04,119 --> 00:04:06,080
Hey, you can cancel
plans with friends

106
00:04:06,121 --> 00:04:08,790
if there's a possibility
for sex.

107
00:04:08,832 --> 00:04:10,417
Phoebe, he's right.
That is the rule.

108
00:04:10,458 --> 00:04:11,960
I don't accept this rule.

109
00:04:12,002 --> 00:04:14,421
When we make plans,
I expect you show up.

110
00:04:14,462 --> 00:04:16,423
Okay? I can't just
be a way to kill time

111
00:04:16,464 --> 00:04:17,925
till you meet
someone better.

112
00:04:17,966 --> 00:04:20,010
You know, boyfriends
and girlfriends

113
00:04:20,052 --> 00:04:22,763
are going to come and go,
but this is for life.

114
00:04:22,804 --> 00:04:24,181
Wow... I'm so sorry.

115
00:04:24,223 --> 00:04:27,101
I had no idea
it would bother you this much.

116
00:04:27,142 --> 00:04:28,643
Well, it does.

117
00:04:28,685 --> 00:04:31,271
Okay, can I make it up
to you, huh?

118
00:04:31,312 --> 00:04:32,606
I'm sorry.

119
00:04:32,647 --> 00:04:34,983
How about dinner tomorrow night?

120
00:04:35,025 --> 00:04:36,610
I'll pay for myself.

121
00:04:38,820 --> 00:04:41,322
Okay, you wore me down.

122
00:04:43,324 --> 00:04:44,826
Hey, Joe,
while you're over there

123
00:04:44,868 --> 00:04:46,912
how about another beer
for "The Ross-a-tron."

124
00:04:46,954 --> 00:04:50,124
The Ross... is that back?

125
00:04:54,753 --> 00:04:55,712
Hi.

126
00:04:55,754 --> 00:04:57,380
The other cheesecake came.

127
00:04:57,422 --> 00:05:00,300
They delivered it
to the wrong address again.

128
00:05:00,341 --> 00:05:02,677
So, just bring it back
downstairs.

129
00:05:02,719 --> 00:05:04,096
What's the problem?

130
00:05:04,138 --> 00:05:06,473
I can't seem to say good-bye.

131
00:05:06,514 --> 00:05:08,016
Are you serious?

132
00:05:08,058 --> 00:05:09,977
Chandler, we ate an entire
cheesecake two days ago

133
00:05:10,018 --> 00:05:11,519
and you want more?

134
00:05:11,561 --> 00:05:14,231
Well, I've forgotten
what it tastes like, okay?

135
00:05:14,273 --> 00:05:16,108
It was cheesecake.

136
00:05:16,150 --> 00:05:17,651
It was fine.

137
00:05:17,692 --> 00:05:21,362
It had a buttery, crumbly,
graham cracker crust

138
00:05:21,404 --> 00:05:24,283
with a very... rich

139
00:05:24,324 --> 00:05:28,495
yet light...
cream cheese filling.

140
00:05:30,705 --> 00:05:33,208
Well, my whole mouth
just filled with saliva.

141
00:05:33,250 --> 00:05:35,335
Okay, you know what?

142
00:05:35,376 --> 00:05:36,461
Forget it.

143
00:05:36,503 --> 00:05:37,504
We are just hungry.

144
00:05:37,545 --> 00:05:38,755
We have not had lunch.

145
00:05:38,797 --> 00:05:40,174
We are just light-headed.

146
00:05:40,215 --> 00:05:41,758
So, let us go out
and have lunch

147
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:43,218
and forget
about the cheesecake.

148
00:05:43,260 --> 00:05:44,845
Yeah, we'll drop it off
downstairs

149
00:05:44,886 --> 00:05:46,263
so we're not tempted.

150
00:05:46,305 --> 00:05:47,681
Good idea. Where do you
want to go to lunch?

151
00:05:47,722 --> 00:05:49,390
Mama's Little Bakery,
Chicago, Illinois.

152
00:05:53,145 --> 00:05:57,774
Oh... Mel Torme died.

153
00:05:57,816 --> 00:05:59,901
Joey, that paper's,
like, a year old.

154
00:05:59,943 --> 00:06:03,864
Oh, does that mean
the Sam Goody sale is over?

155
00:06:03,905 --> 00:06:05,532
Hey.

156
00:06:05,573 --> 00:06:07,117
Hey.
Hey.

157
00:06:07,159 --> 00:06:09,870
So, I finally heard
back from Aunt Cheryl

158
00:06:09,911 --> 00:06:11,788
and apparently
it wasn't a mistake.

159
00:06:11,830 --> 00:06:14,624
Uh, there's-there's
limited seating in the hall...

160
00:06:14,666 --> 00:06:16,584
Limited seating?

161
00:06:16,626 --> 00:06:19,713
I am just one
tiny person.

162
00:06:19,754 --> 00:06:22,883
Well, yeah,
but she doesn't know that.

163
00:06:22,924 --> 00:06:25,260
I mean, the last
time she saw you

164
00:06:25,302 --> 00:06:26,469
you would have turned

165
00:06:26,511 --> 00:06:28,387
one of those little
wedding chairs

166
00:06:28,429 --> 00:06:29,388
into kindling.

167
00:06:29,430 --> 00:06:31,016
Uh... "limited seating."

168
00:06:31,058 --> 00:06:33,268
Oh, that is such
a lame excuse.

169
00:06:33,310 --> 00:06:36,771
That's not the reason
why she's not inviting me.

170
00:06:36,813 --> 00:06:37,981
What's the big deal?

171
00:06:38,023 --> 00:06:39,358
I wasn't even invited
to the ceremony

172
00:06:39,398 --> 00:06:41,235
just the reception,
and you know what?

173
00:06:41,276 --> 00:06:42,819
If it makes you
feel any better

174
00:06:42,861 --> 00:06:45,113
Joan and I will just
make an appearance

175
00:06:45,155 --> 00:06:46,573
and then, and then

176
00:06:46,614 --> 00:06:48,867
we'll-we'll leave
early as a sign
of protest.

177
00:06:48,909 --> 00:06:50,911
Joan?
Yeah, Joan Tedeschi.

178
00:06:50,952 --> 00:06:51,912
My date.

179
00:06:51,953 --> 00:06:53,372
She's an assistant
professor

180
00:06:53,412 --> 00:06:54,915
in the linguistics
department.

181
00:06:54,956 --> 00:06:56,083
Tall, very beautiful

182
00:06:56,124 --> 00:06:58,793
and despite what
some people say

183
00:06:58,835 --> 00:07:00,379
not broad-backed.

184
00:07:00,419 --> 00:07:01,462
Wait a minute.

185
00:07:01,504 --> 00:07:03,882
You got
"Ross Geller and guest"?

186
00:07:03,924 --> 00:07:07,052
I wasn't invited,
and you got "and guest"?

187
00:07:07,094 --> 00:07:08,553
Uh, excuse me...

188
00:07:08,595 --> 00:07:10,638
I do have to interrupt
on Ross's behalf.

189
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:12,391
I think the rule applies here.

190
00:07:12,431 --> 00:07:15,060
Since he has a chance
to get on broad-back...

191
00:07:15,102 --> 00:07:16,436
Not broad-back!

192
00:07:16,477 --> 00:07:18,855
MONICA:
Wait a minute.

193
00:07:18,897 --> 00:07:20,565
You're bringing me.

194
00:07:20,607 --> 00:07:22,525
Well, I can't
cancel on Joan.

195
00:07:22,567 --> 00:07:23,610
Why not?

196
00:07:23,651 --> 00:07:25,362
Because-- did
you not hear me?--

197
00:07:25,404 --> 00:07:27,072
she's an assistant
professor

198
00:07:27,114 --> 00:07:29,283
in the linguistics
department, okay?

199
00:07:29,324 --> 00:07:30,367
They're wild.

200
00:07:30,409 --> 00:07:33,745
Why do you want
to come anyway?

201
00:07:33,787 --> 00:07:34,829
Because...

202
00:07:34,871 --> 00:07:36,706
she's my cousin.

203
00:07:36,748 --> 00:07:39,876
I mean,
we grew up together.

204
00:07:39,918 --> 00:07:41,544
We're family, you know

205
00:07:41,586 --> 00:07:43,588
and that's...
that's important to me.

206
00:07:43,630 --> 00:07:46,800
Okay, all right,
I'll take you.

207
00:07:46,841 --> 00:07:48,760
I'll go call Joan.

208
00:07:48,802 --> 00:07:51,846
Oh, that's nice.

209
00:07:51,888 --> 00:07:53,765
Family should
be there, huh?

210
00:07:53,807 --> 00:07:56,143
This is her wedding;
happiest day of her life.

211
00:07:56,184 --> 00:07:57,978
We'll see.

212
00:08:01,689 --> 00:08:03,233
( Chandler sighs )

213
00:08:03,275 --> 00:08:04,943
Well, thank you for lunch.

214
00:08:04,985 --> 00:08:07,112
Wait a minute. I didn't pay.
I thought you paid.

215
00:08:07,154 --> 00:08:09,948
So, apparently we just don't pay
for food anymore.

216
00:08:09,990 --> 00:08:11,992
( chuckles )

217
00:08:12,033 --> 00:08:13,368
Do you see what I see?

218
00:08:13,410 --> 00:08:14,369
( gasps )

219
00:08:14,411 --> 00:08:16,579
It's still there.

220
00:08:16,621 --> 00:08:18,832
Mrs. Braverman must be out.

221
00:08:22,669 --> 00:08:24,004
She could be
out of town.

222
00:08:24,045 --> 00:08:25,839
Maybe she'll be
gone for months.

223
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:27,715
By then, the cheesecake
may have gone bad.

224
00:08:27,757 --> 00:08:29,717
We don't want
her to come back
to bad cheesecake.

225
00:08:29,759 --> 00:08:30,760
No, that could kill her.

226
00:08:30,802 --> 00:08:31,803
Well, we don't want that.

227
00:08:31,845 --> 00:08:33,096
No, so we're
protecting her.

228
00:08:33,138 --> 00:08:34,139
We should take it.

229
00:08:34,181 --> 00:08:35,307
We should move quick.
Why?

230
00:08:35,349 --> 00:08:36,808
Because I think
I just heard her

231
00:08:36,850 --> 00:08:37,976
moving around in there.

232
00:08:38,018 --> 00:08:39,727
Go, go, go, go, go, go.

233
00:08:41,520 --> 00:08:42,856
( gasps )

234
00:08:42,897 --> 00:08:44,316
Oh, my God, that's David.

235
00:08:44,358 --> 00:08:45,484
David who?

236
00:08:45,525 --> 00:08:47,486
PHOEBE:
David, the
scientist guy.

237
00:08:47,526 --> 00:08:49,321
David that I
was in love with.

238
00:08:49,363 --> 00:08:52,366
David who went to Russia
and broke my heart David.

239
00:08:52,407 --> 00:08:53,741
Oh, my God.

240
00:08:53,783 --> 00:08:55,118
You say someone's name enough

241
00:08:55,160 --> 00:08:56,161
they turn around.

242
00:08:58,663 --> 00:08:59,664
Phoebe.

243
00:08:59,706 --> 00:09:01,791
David.

244
00:09:04,252 --> 00:09:05,837
What's... what are
you doing here?

245
00:09:05,879 --> 00:09:07,506
Aren't you supposed
to be in Russia?

246
00:09:07,547 --> 00:09:09,508
Yeah, I'm just in town
for a conference.

247
00:09:09,549 --> 00:09:11,176
Oh.
Um, God...

248
00:09:11,218 --> 00:09:13,345
You look phenomenal.

249
00:09:13,387 --> 00:09:16,348
Well... yeah.

250
00:09:16,390 --> 00:09:18,058
You look great, too.

251
00:09:18,099 --> 00:09:20,060
Did you get a haircut?

252
00:09:20,101 --> 00:09:22,854
Yeah, well,
I-I-I got, like, 30 of them.

253
00:09:22,896 --> 00:09:24,356
Yeah.

254
00:09:24,398 --> 00:09:26,233
Um, look, I-I-I got
a confession to make.

255
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:27,526
Uh-huh.

256
00:09:27,567 --> 00:09:29,319
I-I was hoping
to run into you here.

257
00:09:29,361 --> 00:09:31,112
I didn't know whether
I should call or not.

258
00:09:31,154 --> 00:09:32,613
I was only in town
for a few days

259
00:09:32,655 --> 00:09:34,574
and, you know, I didn't
want to intrude on your life

260
00:09:34,615 --> 00:09:35,909
or anything like that

261
00:09:35,950 --> 00:09:38,119
but I really
wanted to see you

262
00:09:38,161 --> 00:09:41,164
but I didn't know
if you wanted to see me.

263
00:09:41,206 --> 00:09:44,000
Well... of course I
would want to see you.

264
00:09:44,042 --> 00:09:46,461
I... I think about
you all the time.

265
00:09:46,503 --> 00:09:47,962
Really?

266
00:09:48,004 --> 00:09:50,048
Because I think about you
all the time.

267
00:09:50,090 --> 00:09:51,758
Really?

268
00:09:51,799 --> 00:09:54,428
There's a statue in Minsk
that reminds me of you so much.

269
00:09:54,469 --> 00:09:56,430
I mean, um,
it's actually of Lenin

270
00:09:56,471 --> 00:09:58,390
but-but, you know...

271
00:09:58,432 --> 00:10:00,267
Yeah.
at certain angles...

272
00:10:00,308 --> 00:10:01,726
Um... anyway

273
00:10:01,768 --> 00:10:03,437
do you want
to have dinner tonight?

274
00:10:03,478 --> 00:10:05,146
Yes.

275
00:10:05,188 --> 00:10:06,814
Oh, no.

276
00:10:06,856 --> 00:10:08,442
Oh, uh, what?

277
00:10:08,483 --> 00:10:09,817
I can't.

278
00:10:09,859 --> 00:10:11,194
I can't believe I have plans.
I can't.

279
00:10:11,236 --> 00:10:12,904
Can you do it
tomorrow night, though?

280
00:10:12,946 --> 00:10:15,740
Uh, no, I have to go
in a few hours.

281
00:10:15,782 --> 00:10:17,951
I have to be on the red-eye.

282
00:10:17,992 --> 00:10:20,745
Well, listen, you know,
next time you're in Minsk, um...

283
00:10:20,787 --> 00:10:22,872
Phoebe, can I talk
to you for a second?

284
00:10:22,914 --> 00:10:23,873
Uh-huh.

285
00:10:23,915 --> 00:10:25,833
What are you doing?

286
00:10:25,875 --> 00:10:27,544
Well, I have plans
with Joey tonight.

287
00:10:27,586 --> 00:10:29,629
So? He'll understand.

288
00:10:29,670 --> 00:10:32,591
No, he won't,
and that's not even the point.

289
00:10:32,632 --> 00:10:34,509
Monica, I made a whole speech

290
00:10:34,551 --> 00:10:37,596
about how you do not
cancel plans with friends

291
00:10:37,637 --> 00:10:39,639
and now,
you know, what?

292
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:42,683
Just because potentially
the love of my life

293
00:10:42,725 --> 00:10:45,479
comes back from Russia
just for one night

294
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:47,397
I should change my beliefs?

295
00:10:47,439 --> 00:10:49,316
I should change my beliefs.

296
00:10:49,357 --> 00:10:50,733
No.

297
00:10:50,775 --> 00:10:53,111
No, no. If I don't have
my principles

298
00:10:53,153 --> 00:10:54,571
I don't have anything.

299
00:10:54,613 --> 00:10:56,531
God, you are so strong.

300
00:10:56,573 --> 00:10:58,617
Or, I should rush through dinner
with Joey

301
00:10:58,658 --> 00:11:00,118
and I can meet David at 9:00.

302
00:11:07,334 --> 00:11:09,586
Oh, my God,
that is so good.

303
00:11:09,628 --> 00:11:10,795
I'm full.

304
00:11:10,837 --> 00:11:13,381
And yet I know,
if I stop eating this

305
00:11:13,423 --> 00:11:14,966
I'll regret it.

306
00:11:16,009 --> 00:11:17,135
Hey.

307
00:11:17,177 --> 00:11:18,886
Hey, what have
you got there?

308
00:11:18,928 --> 00:11:20,096
Oh, it's, um...

309
00:11:20,138 --> 00:11:21,181
It's tofu cake.

310
00:11:21,222 --> 00:11:22,223
Do you want some?

311
00:11:22,265 --> 00:11:23,600
( groans )

312
00:11:26,269 --> 00:11:27,354
( sighs )

313
00:11:27,395 --> 00:11:28,396
What are you
doing tonight?

314
00:11:28,438 --> 00:11:30,898
Huh?
Dude, dude.

315
00:11:30,940 --> 00:11:32,025
Oh!

316
00:11:32,066 --> 00:11:33,776
Sorry.

317
00:11:33,818 --> 00:11:36,154
Uh, I got those plans
with Phoebe. Why?

318
00:11:36,196 --> 00:11:37,489
Oh, really?

319
00:11:37,531 --> 00:11:39,240
Monica said she
had a date at 9:00.

320
00:11:39,282 --> 00:11:40,783
What? Tonight?

321
00:11:40,825 --> 00:11:42,076
That's what Monica said.

322
00:11:42,118 --> 00:11:43,578
After she gave me
that big speech

323
00:11:43,620 --> 00:11:45,246
she goes and makes
a date with a guy

324
00:11:45,288 --> 00:11:47,290
on the same night
she has plans with me?

325
00:11:47,332 --> 00:11:49,959
I think she's trying to pull
a fast one on Big Daddy.

326
00:11:56,216 --> 00:11:58,051
Oh, here--
I think this is us.

327
00:11:59,093 --> 00:12:01,596
Limited seating, my ass.

328
00:12:01,638 --> 00:12:04,599
Let's just see
who made the cut.

329
00:12:04,641 --> 00:12:05,850
Hi.
Hi.

330
00:12:05,892 --> 00:12:07,143
I'm Monica Geller.

331
00:12:07,185 --> 00:12:08,978
How do you know
the bride and groom?

332
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:10,397
Oh, I used to work with Frannie.

333
00:12:10,438 --> 00:12:11,565
Used to work with her.

334
00:12:11,606 --> 00:12:12,899
Used to.

335
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:15,026
I'm a relative
and I didn't get invited.

336
00:12:15,068 --> 00:12:16,819
A blood relative.

337
00:12:16,861 --> 00:12:18,071
Blood.

338
00:12:19,573 --> 00:12:22,283
Stop saying blood
to strangers.

339
00:12:23,326 --> 00:12:24,452
So, how about
you, hmm?

340
00:12:24,494 --> 00:12:26,204
How do you know
the happy couple?

341
00:12:26,246 --> 00:12:27,622
We went to college with

342
00:12:27,664 --> 00:12:29,416
both of them,
and now we live next door.

343
00:12:29,457 --> 00:12:32,210
Okay, you're fine.

344
00:12:36,797 --> 00:12:37,798
Hey.
Hey.

345
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:38,966
Are you guys ready?

346
00:12:39,008 --> 00:12:40,759
Yes, I will have
a green salad

347
00:12:40,801 --> 00:12:43,012
house dressing,
and water's fine.

348
00:12:43,054 --> 00:12:44,180
Okay.
Okay.

349
00:12:44,222 --> 00:12:45,306
And for you, sir.

350
00:12:45,348 --> 00:12:46,391
Yeah--

351
00:12:46,433 --> 00:12:48,184
this slow-roasted salmon.

352
00:12:48,226 --> 00:12:50,061
Just how slow are we talking?

353
00:12:51,688 --> 00:12:53,356
It's already been roasted.

354
00:12:53,398 --> 00:12:55,525
Oh, then no.

355
00:12:55,567 --> 00:12:57,402
Maybe I should hear
those specials again.

356
00:12:57,444 --> 00:12:59,320
Oh, Joey, we've
heard the specials

357
00:12:59,362 --> 00:13:00,488
three times, okay?

358
00:13:00,530 --> 00:13:02,323
There's prime rib,
mahi-mahi

359
00:13:02,365 --> 00:13:04,492
and a very special
lobster ravioli.

360
00:13:04,534 --> 00:13:06,620
Actually, we're
out of the lobster ravioli.

361
00:13:06,661 --> 00:13:10,498
Oh, well, that
changes everything.

362
00:13:10,540 --> 00:13:12,751
You know what, Pheebs?
Huh?

363
00:13:12,791 --> 00:13:13,960
You were right before.

364
00:13:14,001 --> 00:13:16,337
Mm-hmm.
Friends are
so important.

365
00:13:16,379 --> 00:13:18,423
Yeah, I'm very
wise, I know.

366
00:13:18,465 --> 00:13:20,467
You know what
I really want?

367
00:13:20,508 --> 00:13:21,509
What?

368
00:13:21,551 --> 00:13:23,678
Is to have a long, long talk.

369
00:13:23,720 --> 00:13:25,804
You know, get Joey
out on the open road

370
00:13:25,846 --> 00:13:28,057
and really open him up.

371
00:13:28,099 --> 00:13:29,684
Any progress?

372
00:13:29,726 --> 00:13:30,769
Yes.

373
00:13:30,809 --> 00:13:33,688
I will have
the lobster ravioli.

374
00:13:33,730 --> 00:13:35,607
Oh, my God, Joey.

375
00:13:35,649 --> 00:13:37,024
This is taking forever.

376
00:13:37,066 --> 00:13:38,859
What's the rush, what?

377
00:13:38,901 --> 00:13:40,278
( stuttering ):
Well, I just...

378
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:42,029
I have, you know,
I have an appointment

379
00:13:42,071 --> 00:13:43,864
and it's very important.

380
00:13:43,906 --> 00:13:45,199
Oh, well, what is it?

381
00:13:45,241 --> 00:13:47,661
Well...

382
00:13:47,702 --> 00:13:49,078
It's a date.

383
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:50,455
A date?

384
00:13:50,497 --> 00:13:51,706
No, no, Pheebs.

385
00:13:51,748 --> 00:13:52,999
You must be mistaken

386
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:54,709
because I know you
wouldn't schedule a date

387
00:13:54,751 --> 00:13:56,753
on the same night you
have plans with a friend.

388
00:13:56,795 --> 00:13:58,797
Come on, Joey, don't make
me feel badly about this.

389
00:13:58,837 --> 00:14:01,549
No, I'm gonna.

390
00:14:01,591 --> 00:14:03,092
That's right, yeah.

391
00:14:03,134 --> 00:14:04,552
You made me feel
really guilty

392
00:14:04,594 --> 00:14:06,012
about going out
with that girl

393
00:14:06,053 --> 00:14:07,846
like I did something
terrible to you.

394
00:14:07,888 --> 00:14:09,848
Now, Pheebs, you're
doing the same thing.

395
00:14:09,890 --> 00:14:11,100
It's not the same thing.

396
00:14:11,142 --> 00:14:12,519
This is totally different.

397
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:13,561
This is with David.

398
00:14:13,603 --> 00:14:14,688
Remember David?

399
00:14:14,729 --> 00:14:16,063
The scientist guy?

400
00:14:16,105 --> 00:14:17,649
He's very special to me.

401
00:14:17,691 --> 00:14:20,193
Okay, well, my girl from
the other night was special.

402
00:14:20,234 --> 00:14:21,402
She was a scientist, too.

403
00:14:21,444 --> 00:14:22,445
She was?

404
00:14:22,487 --> 00:14:24,447
Well, she graduated high school.

405
00:14:24,489 --> 00:14:25,699
Okay, whatever.

406
00:14:25,740 --> 00:14:26,991
You know what?

407
00:14:27,033 --> 00:14:28,368
I don't have time
to convince you

408
00:14:28,409 --> 00:14:29,703
because he's only
here for four hours

409
00:14:29,744 --> 00:14:30,911
and I'm going
to go see him.

410
00:14:30,953 --> 00:14:31,954
Fine!
Yeah.

411
00:14:31,996 --> 00:14:32,747
Yeah.
Fine!

412
00:14:34,749 --> 00:14:36,710
What are you
still doing here?

413
00:14:36,751 --> 00:14:38,628
I told you,
lobster ravioli!

414
00:14:41,214 --> 00:14:42,590
Hey.

415
00:14:42,632 --> 00:14:44,133
Hey, I was just
about to leave.

416
00:14:44,175 --> 00:14:45,719
I didn't think
you were coming.

417
00:14:45,760 --> 00:14:48,346
Oh, I wouldn't
have missed this.

418
00:14:48,388 --> 00:14:50,473
Well, I'm very
glad you're here.

419
00:14:50,515 --> 00:14:52,266
Oh, you're
such a gentleman.

420
00:14:52,308 --> 00:14:54,435
Come on, we're
going to my place.

421
00:14:56,937 --> 00:14:58,565
Mmm.

422
00:15:01,234 --> 00:15:04,779
Are you eating
the cheesecake without me?

423
00:15:04,821 --> 00:15:07,031
Uh-uh.

424
00:15:07,073 --> 00:15:11,035
I will give you $100
to whistle right now.

425
00:15:15,331 --> 00:15:17,208
How could you eat
the cheesecake without me?

426
00:15:17,250 --> 00:15:18,626
Oh, what are
you going to do?

427
00:15:18,668 --> 00:15:19,627
You going to go run

428
00:15:19,669 --> 00:15:20,795
and tell Monica?

429
00:15:20,837 --> 00:15:22,380
Are you going
to tell Joey?

430
00:15:22,422 --> 00:15:24,173
No, because you'd have
to tell them what we did.

431
00:15:24,215 --> 00:15:25,466
We are dessert stealers.

432
00:15:25,508 --> 00:15:26,718
We are living
outside of the law.

433
00:15:26,760 --> 00:15:28,010
You know what?

434
00:15:28,052 --> 00:15:29,637
I don't trust you
with this cake anymore.

435
00:15:29,679 --> 00:15:30,680
And I got it first.

436
00:15:30,722 --> 00:15:32,139
And I'm taking it back.
What?

437
00:15:32,181 --> 00:15:33,307
What?

438
00:15:33,349 --> 00:15:34,934
No, no, no, you don't.

439
00:15:34,975 --> 00:15:36,935
Oh, yes!
You think I
trust you with it?

440
00:15:36,977 --> 00:15:38,312
No, we're going to split it.

441
00:15:38,354 --> 00:15:39,647
You take half and I take half.

442
00:15:39,689 --> 00:15:40,648
That's not fair.

443
00:15:40,690 --> 00:15:41,733
You've already had some.

444
00:15:41,775 --> 00:15:43,150
Oh, then, you know what?

445
00:15:43,192 --> 00:15:44,903
I think Monica would be
very interested to know

446
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:47,988
that you called
her cheesecake dry and mealy.

447
00:15:48,030 --> 00:15:49,490
What do we use to split it?

448
00:15:49,532 --> 00:15:50,450
Okay.

449
00:15:53,578 --> 00:15:54,871
All right, pick a half.

450
00:15:54,913 --> 00:15:55,954
Okay.

451
00:15:55,996 --> 00:15:59,542
Well, this side looks bigger.

452
00:15:59,584 --> 00:16:00,794
Mm-hmm.

453
00:16:00,835 --> 00:16:03,170
But there's more crust
on this side.

454
00:16:03,212 --> 00:16:04,297
You know?

455
00:16:04,338 --> 00:16:05,506
So, maybe if I measured...

456
00:16:05,548 --> 00:16:06,925
For God's sake,
just pick a piece!

457
00:16:06,966 --> 00:16:08,217
I pick that one.

458
00:16:08,259 --> 00:16:11,512
Ha, so the smaller piece.

459
00:16:11,554 --> 00:16:12,722
Okay.

460
00:16:12,764 --> 00:16:13,890
There you go.

461
00:16:13,932 --> 00:16:15,934
Enjoy your half, my friend.

462
00:16:15,974 --> 00:16:17,017
But that is it.

463
00:16:17,059 --> 00:16:19,061
No sharing, no switching

464
00:16:19,103 --> 00:16:20,521
and don't come crying to me

465
00:16:20,563 --> 00:16:22,857
if you eat your piece too fast.

466
00:16:22,899 --> 00:16:25,777
( screams )

467
00:16:27,862 --> 00:16:30,197
Oh...

468
00:16:30,239 --> 00:16:32,617
Oh!

469
00:16:32,659 --> 00:16:35,411
All right, you got to give me
some of your piece.

470
00:16:35,453 --> 00:16:37,163
Oh, no, no.

471
00:16:37,204 --> 00:16:40,374
No switching, no sharing,
and don't come crying to me!

472
00:16:40,416 --> 00:16:41,918
Ha, ha, ha.

473
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:44,879
I may just sit here
and have my cake all day.

474
00:16:44,921 --> 00:16:46,923
Just sit here in
the hallway and eat my...

475
00:16:59,727 --> 00:17:01,938
Ross, sweetheart!

476
00:17:01,980 --> 00:17:04,148
Oh, hey, Aunt Millie.

477
00:17:04,190 --> 00:17:06,651
Isn't it a beautiful wedding?

478
00:17:06,693 --> 00:17:08,027
Yes, yes it is.

479
00:17:12,365 --> 00:17:14,575
Every time on the lips.

480
00:17:14,617 --> 00:17:17,077
Why, why on the lips?

481
00:17:17,119 --> 00:17:20,247
( applause )

482
00:17:20,289 --> 00:17:21,374
There's Frannie.

483
00:17:21,415 --> 00:17:22,834
Won't she be happy to see me?

484
00:17:22,876 --> 00:17:24,042
Now, wait a minute.

485
00:17:24,084 --> 00:17:25,461
You be nice, all right?

486
00:17:25,503 --> 00:17:27,630
I didn't bring you here
so you could ambush her.

487
00:17:27,672 --> 00:17:29,799
Frannie was the one
who found your Playboys

488
00:17:29,841 --> 00:17:31,009
and showed them to Mom.

489
00:17:31,050 --> 00:17:32,426
That bitch.

490
00:17:37,306 --> 00:17:39,017
Monica!

491
00:17:39,058 --> 00:17:40,226
What...

492
00:17:40,267 --> 00:17:41,435
Am I doing here?

493
00:17:41,477 --> 00:17:42,729
Why? Surprised to see me?

494
00:17:42,770 --> 00:17:43,771
Ross brought me.

495
00:17:43,813 --> 00:17:45,398
How do you like that?

496
00:17:45,439 --> 00:17:48,108
Hi, Frannie,
congratulations.

497
00:17:49,819 --> 00:17:50,987
You invite my brother

498
00:17:51,029 --> 00:17:52,488
you invite my whole
family and not me?

499
00:17:52,530 --> 00:17:53,781
Why?

500
00:17:53,823 --> 00:17:55,408
Why wouldn't you want
me at your wedding?

501
00:17:55,449 --> 00:17:56,826
What could I
have possibly done?

502
00:17:58,327 --> 00:18:00,538
Stuart.

503
00:18:00,580 --> 00:18:03,249
I believe you
know my husband.

504
00:18:04,333 --> 00:18:05,793
So it's really
a question of

505
00:18:05,835 --> 00:18:08,838
who could you
have possibly done?

506
00:18:16,888 --> 00:18:19,807
Oh, I hate this,
but I have to go.

507
00:18:19,849 --> 00:18:21,935
I can't miss my flight.

508
00:18:21,976 --> 00:18:23,477
Are you sure?

509
00:18:23,519 --> 00:18:25,813
I bet there's another
flight to Minsk in...
July.

510
00:18:28,024 --> 00:18:35,197
( speaking Russian )

511
00:18:35,239 --> 00:18:37,658
That's really beautiful.

512
00:18:37,700 --> 00:18:38,993
What does it mean?

513
00:18:39,035 --> 00:18:41,746
Please clean my beakers.

514
00:18:41,788 --> 00:18:44,331
I don't get out
of the lab much.

515
00:18:44,373 --> 00:18:45,792
( giggles )

516
00:18:45,833 --> 00:18:48,294
I thought it meant...

517
00:18:48,335 --> 00:18:50,170
something else.

518
00:18:50,212 --> 00:18:51,839
Yeah, I, well,
I really, actually

519
00:18:51,881 --> 00:18:55,259
wanted to say, um, that.

520
00:18:55,301 --> 00:18:57,595
But I figured
I probably shouldn't

521
00:18:57,637 --> 00:18:59,555
because, you know

522
00:18:59,597 --> 00:19:01,682
I have to leave.

523
00:19:01,724 --> 00:19:03,350
No, you're right,
you're right.

524
00:19:03,392 --> 00:19:05,394
Don't say it.

525
00:19:05,436 --> 00:19:09,023
I do, though.

526
00:19:09,065 --> 00:19:12,192
I do, too.

527
00:19:21,201 --> 00:19:22,369
Bye, Phoebe.

528
00:19:22,411 --> 00:19:24,246
Bye.

529
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:35,549
Okay, now's not the time,
Joey, all right?

530
00:19:35,591 --> 00:19:37,384
You can yell at me tomorrow.

531
00:19:37,426 --> 00:19:38,552
No, no, no, Pheebs.

532
00:19:38,594 --> 00:19:40,304
I'm not going to yell at you.

533
00:19:40,346 --> 00:19:44,934
I just, you know, started
thinking about you and David

534
00:19:44,976 --> 00:19:47,561
and I remember how bummed you
were the first time he left.

535
00:19:47,603 --> 00:19:49,730
I just...

536
00:19:49,772 --> 00:19:51,732
Oh, Pheebs, come here.

537
00:19:51,774 --> 00:19:54,234
Are you okay?

538
00:19:54,276 --> 00:19:56,362
No, I'm not okay.

539
00:19:56,403 --> 00:19:58,322
The only guy I've
ever been crazy about

540
00:19:58,364 --> 00:20:03,577
is going to Minsk and I
may never see him again.

541
00:20:03,619 --> 00:20:05,412
Hey, you know,
you could always visit him.

542
00:20:05,454 --> 00:20:06,580
Oh, right--
like they're

543
00:20:06,622 --> 00:20:08,206
going to let me
have a passport.

544
00:20:08,248 --> 00:20:10,668
Is there anything I can do?

545
00:20:10,710 --> 00:20:12,378
Whatever you need.

546
00:20:13,420 --> 00:20:16,423
Well, but now

547
00:20:16,465 --> 00:20:18,592
if you could achieve
positronic distillation

548
00:20:18,634 --> 00:20:20,469
of subatomic particles,
you know

549
00:20:20,511 --> 00:20:22,680
before he does, then
he could come back.

550
00:20:29,311 --> 00:20:31,647
I could give it a shot.

551
00:20:34,567 --> 00:20:37,277
Oh, yeah.
Okay.

552
00:20:37,319 --> 00:20:38,654
Oh, yay, look.

553
00:20:38,696 --> 00:20:40,489
There's a piece that
doesn't have floor on it.

554
00:20:40,531 --> 00:20:42,158
Stick to your side.

555
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:43,450
Come on, now.

556
00:20:55,213 --> 00:20:57,339
All right,
what are we having?

557
00:21:04,931 --> 00:21:05,932
Oh, wait.

558
00:21:05,973 --> 00:21:06,891
I forgot my wrap.

559
00:21:06,933 --> 00:21:08,684
Okay, wait here.

560
00:21:26,452 --> 00:21:27,536
Hi, sweetie!

561
00:21:27,578 --> 00:21:29,122
Are you leaving?

562
00:21:29,163 --> 00:21:31,124
Well...
Give us a kiss.

563
00:21:31,165 --> 00:21:32,208
Come on.

564
00:21:32,250 --> 00:21:33,960
( groans )

565
00:21:34,001 --> 00:21:35,502
Come on.

566
00:21:40,841 --> 00:21:42,009
Why?!

567
00:21:42,051 --> 00:21:44,053
Why on the lips?!

